{
  "$comment": "Swift<->JS public-surface parity map. Keys under `symbols` are CadenceCore selectors as check-parity.mjs extracts them (funcs keyed with external labels; stored fields and enum cases are out of scope in v1). A value is the JS export twin (string), {\"js\": export, \"note\": why-the-shape-differs}, or {\"swiftOnly\": reason}. `webOnly` lists JS exports with no Swift twin. `exhaustiveJs: true` means every export of `js` must be accounted for.",
